<title>SWEDEN: Trading in Marieberg suspended - bourse.</title>
<headline>Trading in Marieberg suspended - bourse.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in Swedish media company Tidning AB Marieberg was suspended on Thursday morning, the Stockholm bourse announced.  </p>
<p>The group, which owns newspapers and runs tableware company Duni, was last traded at 175 crowns, two crowns higher than Wednesday's close.</p>
<p>Marieberg, controlled by Swedish media family Bonniers, is due to report its nine month results on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
